# WS1-04. Source: spec/02-types.md §9 (a literal operand takes the other
# operand's type when it fits) and §10 (wrapping two's-complement): u8 200+100=44,
# u16 65535+1=0, i8 127+1=-128.
expect: output
contrast: x + 100; ==> x + 50;
contrast-expect: output
--- output
44 0 -128
--- contrast-output
250 0 -128
